WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:04.370
- My love of kites started
about 20 years ago.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.230
I taught math for 35 years.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.810
I just combined the two to try
to reach all of my students.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.850
I figured, why not take this
whole math lesson outside?

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.933
Maybe, just maybe, they
would see the relationship.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.200
- My name is Winfred Randolph Lowe,

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.040
but in Delray on the beach
when I'm flying my kites,

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.241
they call me Randy The Kite Man.

00:00:30.241 --> 00:00:33.620
(upbeat music)

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.940
I started flying kites 20 years ago.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.290
I bought my first kite,
and I never looked back.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.910
I fly my kites as much as possible.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.943
I have about 60 or 70 kites.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.200
On any particular given
day, you can paint the sky

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.823
with sea creatures, whales, scuba divers.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.320
You're not only looking at the kite,

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.020
but you're looking at the strings.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.670
There's math there, and you
can do something with it.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.570
Kites are geometric figures,
kites are triangles.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.040
And that is one of the things

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.700
that I tried to take advantage of.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.380
Instead of doing it in
the classroom at desks,

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.753
we take them out in the field.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:18.510
Pythagorean theorem is a formula used

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:22.000
to determine sides of triangles.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.950
If we want to use Pythagorean
theorem on a beach

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.450
as we're trying to fly a kite,

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.610
and we let the kite go and
it travels up the line,

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.700
better known as the hypotenuse.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.950
If we draw a line from the top of the kite

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.770
down to the bottom, that's side A.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.400
If we draw another line from that point,

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.093
back to where we let the kite
go, that would be side B.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.510
So by plugging those
numbers into the triangle,

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:50.550
we have just figured out
how long our string is

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.173
from where we are standing
to the top of the kite.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.480
There's your answer.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.740
We could do fractions,
common denominators,

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.320
uncommon denominators, the more
complicated the numbers are,

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.653
the more math there is.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.890
I retired six years ago.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:07.940
We get a lot of families
that come on Delray Beach,

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.490
and they have kids, and I teach math.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.333
I tell them, "See that right there?

00:02:14.857 --> 00:02:17.390
"We can do a math problem
with that," you know?

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:20.370
And some kids understand, "Oh
yeah, we did that in school."

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.360
Nowadays, they see it.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.223
But for a lot of the younger kids,

00:02:25.223 --> 00:02:26.820
it gets them thinking, too.

